# legacy evaluation corpus binaries (now migrated into user-data storage
# by `legolization corpus`; kept only as a one-way migration source) + run
# output
data/corpus/meshes/
data/corpus/synthetic/
eval/runs/
eval/profiles/
/eval/stablelego
/eval/datasets
# pair renders and review pages (scripts/render_pairs.py, review_pairs.py);
# the judged verdicts themselves are TRACKED at references/aesthetic-preferences
/eval/preferences

# default corpus evaluation output (legolization corpus collect/assemble/evaluate)
legolization-eval/

# external validation datasets fetched by scripts/fetch_datasets.py and
# scripts/fetch_omr.py. scripts/datasets.toml + datasets.lock.toml are the
# committed truth; the payloads themselves are never committed.
#
# The dataset/eval-output entries above and here deliberately drop the trailing
# slash. A `foo/` pattern is directory-only, so it does NOT match a symlink
# (`datasets` is one, pointing at an external volume) and does not match a path
# that does not exist yet. `/foo` matches a directory, a symlink, or a file,
# present or absent — so the protection holds before the first fetch, not just
# after it. tests/test_datasets.py pins both properties.
/datasets
